      "hints": [
        "Recall $-1 \\le \\cos(2x) \\le 1$.",
        "Evaluate $\\frac{3}{2}(-1) + \\frac{1}{2}$ and $\\frac{3}{2}(1) + \\frac{1}{2}$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Use the range of the cosine function $-1 \\le \\cos(2x) \\le 1$ on the domain $0 \\le x \\le \\pi$.",
        "Calculate the minimum and maximum values of $f(x) = \\frac{3}{2}\\cos(2x) + \\frac{1}{2}$:\n$$\\text{Minimum} = \\frac{3}{2}(-1) + \\frac{1}{2} = -1$$\n$$\\text{Maximum} = \\frac{3}{2}(1) + \\frac{1}{2} = 2$$",
        "State the range of $f$:\n$$-1 \\le f(x) \\le 2$$"
      ],
      "checking": {
